  (label "VREF" (at 248.92 369.57 90) (fields_autoplaced)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid d9d45893-56dc-5813-a837-0a8d3b482aaf)
  )
  (text "AUDIO OUT (authentic Model 1 sound, no clean mode). Everything here runs on the quiet +4V5A rail around VREF = 2.25V, grounded to GNDA.\n1. 2.2k load on MOL / MOR, as in the Mega Amp, so the chip's DAC works as it did in the console.\n2. Model 1 style low-pass: inverting OPA2350 stage, 47k in, 100k || 470pF feedback. First order, 3.39 kHz, gain about 2.1.\n   That matches the 47k / 1nF Model 1 filter used by MIDIbox. Change C to 560pF for 2.84 kHz (the VA3 knee) after the A/B test in M4.\n3. Balanced line outs: cold = filter out, hot = filter out inverted again by a 10k / 10k OPA2350 stage. 100 ohm + 10uF + 100k bleed\n   on each leg into a Neutrik 1/4in TRS (tip hot, ring cold, sleeve to GNDA through a 0 ohm ground-lift footprint).\n4. Headphones: 10uF DC block, dual slide pot on its 6-pin plug (volume, headphones only), 1uF + 100k re-bias to VREF, NJM4556A buffer,\n   220uF + 10 ohm into the front 3.5 mm jack. 10k bleeds the output cap so plugging in doesn't pop." (at 25.4 20.32 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 79d264ee-db23-5ac2-ad7a-184236cd072b)
  )
)
